Netserpent is a third-party-hack-program framework under network 3rd
level. It configurably hijacks the 3rd level connections(currently
support tcp) outgoing or forwarding, and configurably use plugins to
determine how to hack the hijacked connection. You can write your own
plugins to :
 - log network sessions
 - transparently do network proxy for up-level programms. Even use
 the shiped chain plugin to chain these plugins together in order to
 make up a network proxy chain
 - analyse some non-open 3rd level network protocal
 - any tricks you can imagine

Download URL
ftp://ftp.fedora.cn/pub/fedora-cn/in-review/distfiles/netserpent-0.1.0.tar.gz

README online
http://blog.chinaunix.net/u/8057/showart.php?id=241665

INSTALL online
http://blog.chinaunix.net/u/8057/showart.php?id=241706

filter plugin writing tutorial
http://blog.chinaunix.net/u/8057/showart.php?id=242123

Currently this project hasn't registed in sourceforge or otherwhere,
if you have any suggestion or be interest on this, just contact me 
freely :

E-MAIL/GTALK: hellwolf DOT misty AT gmail DOT com

--
http://hellwolf.cublog.cn
gpg --keyserver pgp.mit.edu --recv-key 0x6B174C6F

Most of our lives are about proving something, either to ourselves or to
someone else.

