Howdy,

We are pleased to extend an invitation for you to apply for our
upcoming Sun Studio 12 Early Access evaluation program. This 8-week
program is scheduled to begin this week.  Click the following link to
sign up:

   https://feedbackprograms.sun.com/callout/default.html?callid=174B8753F960493192728C9259A02055

Sun Studio software, available for free on Solaris and Linux
platforms, includes the following:

   Parallelizing C, C++, and Fortran compilers
   Code-level debugger
   Memory debugger
   Performance profiling
   OpenMP support
   IDE
   Optimized libraries
   Thread analysis

By joining this Early Access program, you will have the opportunity to
evaluate the new capabilities of Sun Studio software including:

 * Next-generation IDE based on NetBeans 5.5.1 software
 * Improved binary application performance for all platforms- SPARC
and x86/x64
 * Comprehensive support for the Linux OS, including C, C++, Fortran
compilers and tools
 * Ability to debug (dbx) higher levels of optimized code
 * Increased GCC compatibility
 * Thread Analyzer -- a new tool for dynamic detection of common multi-
threading errors.

Thank you for your continued support!

/kso

